A disabled node and a menu button on AT-SPI (docs/plans/20261031-e2e-ui-and-coverage.md Task 6). AccessKit's mapping
gave every node whose role takes no read-only state (a button, a menu item) Enabled and Sensitive even when it was
disabled, and folded disabled into ReadOnly for the others; a button whose `has_popup` is a menu mapped to a plain push
button. Here a disabled node has neither Enabled nor Sensitive whatever its role, ReadOnly marks a read-only node only
(AT-SPI's ReadOnly is an enabled, sensitive object whose value cannot change), a disabled field is not Editable, and a
button with a menu is a PushButtonMenu with HasPopup (a toggle button stays a ToggleButton). An upstream candidate
(AccessKit); it can go when a release carries it.

